# Commits that changed layout and nothing else. `git blame` skips these and
# reports the commit that actually wrote the line.
#
# GitHub reads this file on its own. Local git does not, and needs telling once
# per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# That lives in .git/config, so it does not survive a fresh clone. CLAUDE.md's
# environment section lists it with the other two that bite the same way.
#
# Only add a commit here that a formatter produced and a human did not touch.
# A commit holding one real change among a thousand reformatted lines makes
# blame lie in the one direction nobody would think to check.

